WEBVTT

00:00:00.087 --> 00:00:01.052
Same burger.

00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:02.945
Nearly four times the price.

00:00:02.955 --> 00:00:06.115
In July 2026, a Big Mac cost

00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:10.342
$9.04 in Switzerland, but just $2.38 in

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:11.861
Indonesia.

00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:15.489
In America, the same burger cost $6.22.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:17.079
And it gets stranger:

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:20.343
The Economist magazine
has tracked this one

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.355
burger's price since 1986.

00:00:22.487 --> 00:00:24.877
So why would an economics magazine follow

00:00:24.887 --> 00:00:25.712
a burger?

00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:26.727
To test money.

00:00:26.737 --> 00:00:28.850
Where a Big Mac costs less in

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.819
dollars, that country's
currency may be undervalued.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:36.511
By this measure, Indonesia's
rupiah looked about

00:00:36.521 --> 00:00:37.871
62% undervalued.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.141
Not bad for an idea that began

00:00:40.151 --> 00:00:42.051
as a light-hearted guide.
